WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.120
Here's an indigestion tablet.

2
00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.180
Its active ingredient
is calcium carbonate.

3
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:08.080
Drop it into water and it just sits there.

4
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.540
Calcium carbonate is insoluble.

5
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:16.420
But a titration needs the sample in solution,
reacting as drops fall from a burette.

6
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:20.420
So how can you titrate a tablet
that won't even dissolve in water?

7
00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:24.320
In this mission, you'll follow a
tablet's analysis step by step,

8
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:27.060
keeping track of the moles at every stage.

9
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.640
Then you'll dilute a solution,
pipette out one portion,

10
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.820
and scale your answer back
up to the whole flask.

11
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:38.520
Your mission: find out how to titrate
a tablet that won't dissolve in water,

12
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.440
and work out how pure it is. 